          "compare_47": "Yes",
          "compare_48": "How to decide",
          "compare_49": "<strong>JrTrack 5 Renewed</strong> if you are not sure the whole idea will stick, or it is a first watch for a younger child who may lose it. Same features, a third of the price, certified and warranted.",
          "compare_50": "<strong>JrTrack 5 SE</strong> if you want the current generation without paying for the display. It is the volume choice for a reason.",
          "compare_51": "<strong>JrTrack Pro</strong> if the child is older and will type a lot, if a bulky watch has already been rejected once, or if you want the biggest battery in the lineup.",
          "compare_52": "<b>The plan costs the same on all three.</b> The device price is the only lever, and it is a one-time one.",
